
AWS EC2 to S3 Secure Application Integration

This project configures secure programmatic storage access for an application hosted on an Amazon EC2 instance (devops-ec2) to interact with a private Amazon S3 bucket (devops-s3-139373540961). Access is managed using IAM roles and policies to eliminate hardcoded credentials.

Architectural Components

• Compute: devops-ec2 (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS instance).
• Storage: devops-s3-139373540961 (Private bucket with public access blocked).
• Identity & Access: devops-role assuming an instance profile linked to a custom IAM privilege statement.

Step-by-Step Implementation Guide


1. SSH Key Management & Access Setup

Generate an administrative RSA cryptographic key pair on the management host and inject the public signature onto the target instance to establish trust.
bash
# Generate the cryptographic keypair locally
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 2048 -f ~/.ssh/id_rsa -N ""

# Inject the public signature cleanly via an automated SSM run command block
export INSTANCE_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-instances --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=devops-ec2" --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].InstanceId" --output text --region us-east-1)

cat << EOF > ssm-commands.json
{
  "commands": [
    "mkdir -p /root/.ssh",
    "echo '$(cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub)' >> /root/.ssh/authorized_keys",
    "chmod 700 /root/.ssh",
    "chmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys"
  ]
}
EOF

aws ssm send-command \
  --instance-ids "$INSTANCE_ID" \
  --document-name "AWS-RunShellScript" \
  --parameters file://ssm-commands.json \
  --region us-east-1
Use code with caution.

2. Private S3 Bucket Deployment

Provision the dedicated object storage bucket and apply strict configurations to block all public access paths.
bash
# Provision the bucket namespace
aws s3api create-bucket \
  --bucket devops-s3-139373540961 \
  --region us-east-1

# Apply strict public access control blocks
aws s3api put-public-access-block \
  --bucket devops-s3-139373540961 \
  --public-access-block-configuration BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true \
  --region us-east-1
Use code with caution.

3. Least-Privilege IAM Infrastructure

Build the data policy parameters, create an execution role for EC2, and attach it to the instance workspace.
bash
# Generate the application data boundary policy
cat << 'EOF' > s3-policy.json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject", "s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::devops-s3-139373540961", "arn:aws:s3:::devops-s3-139373540961/*"]
    }
  ]
}
EOF

# Generate the STS AssumeRole trust policy boundary
cat << 'EOF' > trust-policy.json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Service": "://amazonaws.com" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
EOF

# Deploy the configuration assets across the cluster management plane
aws iam create-policy --policy-name devops-s3-policy --policy-document file://s3-policy.json
aws iam create-role --role-name devops-role --assume-role-policy-document file://trust-policy.json
aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name devops-role --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::139373540961:policy/devops-s3-policy

# Link structural assets to the targeted instance configuration matrix
aws iam create-instance-profile --instance-profile-name devops-instance-profile-group
aws iam add-role-to-instance-profile --instance-profile-name devops-instance-profile-group --role-name devops-role

# Map the active structural profile payload to your running EC2 machine instance
aws ec2 associate-iam-instance-profile --instance-id $INSTANCE_ID --iam-instance-profile Name=devops-instance-profile-group --region us-east-1
Use code with caution.

